  "title": "Quadratic Formula & Completing the Square",
  "content": "<p><strong>Quadratic formula:</strong> \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\). Works for any quadratic \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\).</p><p><strong>Completing the square:</strong> Write \\(x^2 + bx\\) as \\((x + \\frac{b}{2})^2 - (\\frac{b}{2})^2\\). Useful for finding the turning point.</p><p><strong>Discriminant</strong> \\(b^2 - 4ac\\): positive = 2 real roots, zero = 1 repeated root, negative = no real roots.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Solve</strong> \\(x^2 + 6x + 2 = 0\\) by completing the square</p><p>\\((x+3)^2 - 9 + 2 = 0\\)</p><p>\\((x+3)^2 = 7\\)</p><p>\\(x = -3 \\pm \\sqrt{7}\\)</p>"
